cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its measured thresholds, cite the repository and the dataset it validates on."
title: "Poomsae Coach: a self-referenced joint-angle form checker for Taekwondo poomsae"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahmadalzaro1/poomsae-coach"
abstract: >-
  A poomsae form checker that separates measurement tolerance from fault attribution: each
  athlete is compared against their own median joint deviation, so a systematic style or camera
  bias is reported as style rather than as a mistake. Includes a four-arm certification of the
  resulting gate, the published detector floor, a frame-by-frame measurement of the mask against
  the dataset's own annotations on all eight forms (with the frames the 2D estimator cannot see
  reported rather than averaged), and machine-checked claims.
keywords:
  - taekwondo
  - poomsae
  - pose estimation
  - DTW
  - measurement uncertainty
  - sports analytics
authors:
  - family-names: Alzaro
    given-names: Ahmad
references:
